From 82211e5d178827ba47f1d2b529f64a30b72676cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 21 Jul 2026 00:16:37 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Gatekeeper: move do_reaper_gk_cgi + helpers OUT of #ifdef
 RTCONFIG_REAPER_MCP (noMCP build fix)

The Gatekeeper CGI and its helpers were inadvertently placed between the rmcp
KDF helpers and rmcp_require_code, i.e. INSIDE the RTCONFIG_REAPER_MCP block.
The MCP image built fine (function present), but the noMCP image compiled the
function out while its mime_handlers registration (not gated) remained, giving
`web.c: 'do_reaper_gk_cgi' undeclared here`. Relocated the whole gk block to
just before the `#ifdef RTCONFIG_REAPER_MCP` so it ships in both images; the
rmcp region (helpers + require_code + do_reaper_mcp_cgi) is unchanged. No
behavioral change to either image. Both MCP and noMCP now build MAKE_EXIT=0.

RULE: any reaper-added, non-MCP-gated CGI/helper must live OUTSIDE the
RTCONFIG_REAPER_MCP ifdef - the MCP build will hide this class of mistake.
